[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n4_choira"
text = "# DRAFT
# Brother Wulfric on the south walk at dusk (night 4, fog), rubbing his knees. The oldest of the choir; crabbed.
# His last talk: ordinary, and a little sad. (He is killed in the fog on the round tonight. Nothing here says so.)
== start
(Old Brother Wulfric on the south walk, a shape in the fog until you're close. He's rubbing his knees.)
Wulfric: Fog. My knees had it before the bell this morning. Forty years, and they've never once been wrong.
-> topics

== again
Wulfric: Still here, boy? Go and ring something.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n4_choira_fast] How are you bearing the fast, brother? -> fast
* [if not n4_choira_came] How did you come to the abbey, brother? -> came

== fast [set n4_choira_fast]
Wulfric: Better than the young ones. I've kept every Lent since before you were born. An empty belly's a quiet one.
(His stomach growls. He ignores it.)
-> topics

== came [set n4_choira_came]
Wulfric: My mother walked me to that gate when I was eleven, with a cheese for the cellarer.
Wulfric: Anselm let us in. He had both his eyes then.
Wulfric: I've not been past Aldgate since. I meant to see the sea again, once, before the end.
Wulfric: Well. There's time yet.
-> topics

== leave
Wulfric: On the mark tonight, boy. Don't keep my knees waiting.
"
